BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Launch: AT BEST\, A MAN\, by Nkiru Okoh
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T150000
UID:bm-5713020260704@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/Nkiru_Oko
 h_Book_Launch__At_Best__A_Man_Flyer_2C.png?cb=1781902146
DESCRIPTION:Join Nkiru Okoh\, a local Nigerian Canadian writer and lawyer\
 , for the launch of her new novel\, AT BEST\, A MAN.\nNkiru explores in he
 r works of fiction themes of identity\, relationships\, and emotional inhe
 ritances that shape how we love. Set in Toronto\, New Jersey\, and Lagos\,
  AT BEST\, A MAN centres on Dayo Lufadeju\, a rising\, emotionally distant
  executive in Toronto. It follows his relationships with his girlfriend an
 d father\, and is about what we inherit\, the things we steal away\, and t
 he vulnerability of being fully known.\n*Featured titles\, including AT BE
 ST\, A MAN and Nkiru's 2024 novel SIX MINUTES TO BLOOM will be available f
 or purchase at the event.\nAdmission: Free. Everyone is welcome!
LOCATION:777 Bathurst St.
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOOK LAUNCH: NAHLIYA AND THE LADY\, by Treslyn Vassel and Sahle Ro
 binson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T160000
UID:bm-5716920260711@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/Nahliyaan
 dtheLady_T.Vassel_Book_LaunchFLyer.png?cb=1781989240
DESCRIPTION:Come celebrate local authors Treslyn Vassel and Sahle Robinson
  (illustrator) and their new picture book\, NAHLIYA AND THE LADY! In this 
 heartfelt story about reunion\, forgiveness\, and finding home\, Nahliya i
 s finally reunited with the Lady--in a new country\, with new fears. As th
 ey build a home from faded memories\, she discovers the courage to forgive
  and open her heart to love again.\nNAHLIYA AND THE LADY is on sale now at
  A Different Booklist\, and will be available for purchase at the event.\n
 Free to attend. Fun for the whole family - see you there!
LOCATION:779 Bathurst St
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOOK LAUNCH: PARSA'S PITHAS\, by Sumaiya Matin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T160000
UID:bm-5713120260725@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/Parsas_Pi
 thas.png?cb=1781904218
DESCRIPTION:You're invited to celebrate the Toronto launch of Sumaiya Mati
 n's debut picture book\, PARSA'S PITHAS!\nSeven-year-old Parsa is struggl
 ing with an art project for school. When she joins her Ma in the kitchen t
 o prepare pithas for the Bengali New Year (Pohela Boishakhi Mela)\, she fa
 ces new obstacles. Engaging with the folk art of pitha making\, she learns
  to tap into her own creative superpower--and there is no stopping her aft
 er that!\n*PARSA'S PITHAS\, by Sumaiya Matin and Nesba Yousef (illus.) wil
 l be available for purchase at the event.\nThis book celebrates Bengali he
 ritage and will make a great addition to any home or school library.\nAdmi
 ssion: Free. Fun for the whole family - all are welcome!
LOCATION:777 Bathurst St.
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
